    description: "The consumer-time io-boundary classification is the canonical path (WI-puvun REFRAME: io_boundary is derived at CLI time, 0 producers stamp it). Both cmd_io_boundaries (cli.py ~4068) and cmd_verify_claims (cli.py ~4761) rehydrate a 4-field _Edge(src,dst,edge_type,meta) from the serialized behavior_map, DROPPING is_resolved and dst_ref. compute_boundary_map reads getattr(edge,'is_resolved',True) (io_boundary.py:1174, the ADR-0028 F3-Filter-1 unresolved-receiver skip) and getattr(edge,'dst_ref',None) (io_boundary.py:1191/1612, the WI-tihup structured lookup). With the facade omitting both, is_resolved defaults True and dst_ref defaults None, so the receiver gate NEVER fires on the CLI path and every unresolved bare-name method match (duck-typed .read()/.write()/.close() on an unknown receiver) is (mis)classified as external_potential — re-inflating exactly the noise INV-tapat/INV-maluk (io-boundary:F3) suppressed in-process. Self-corpus: facade external_potential ~26338 vs faithful 0; the real boundary set (total_io_edges) is unchanged (dst_ref-carrying edges like os.remove classify via the WI-tihup path regardless). Fix: rehydrate is_resolved + dst_ref (ExternalRef.from_dict) in both facades (extract a shared helper). Wave-3 Phase-2 §C io-boundary F1 (facade repair). Subsumes ~96% of WI-pimun (file-node-src chains ~288->12 once external_potential stops dominating). Empirically verified: /tmp/iof1 fixture (os.remove + obj.read() + bus.write()) facade external_potential_edges=2 total=1 vs faithful external_potential_edges=0 total=1."  # 015a
    fields: {}  # 015a
